{"id":306,"flavor":[{"games":["Shield"],"text":"Long ago, there was a king who wore a helmet meant to resemble the head of an Aggron. He was trying to channel the Pokémon’s strength."},{"games":["Sword"],"text":"Aggron has a horn sharp enough to perforate thick iron sheets. It brings down its opponents by ramming into them horn first."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire"],"text":"Aggron is protective of its environment. If its mountain is ravaged by a landslide or a fire, this Pokémon will haul topsoil to the area, plant trees, and beautifully restore its own territory."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","Ruby"],"text":"Aggron claims an entire mountain as its own territory. It mercilessly beats up anything that violates its environment. This Pokémon vigilantly patrols its territory at all times."},{"games":["Y","White","Black","Platinum","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"While seeking iron for food, it digs tunnels by breaking through bedrock with its steel horns."},{"games":["X","White 2","Black 2"],"text":"It claims an entire mountain as its own. The more wounds it has, the more it has battled, so don’t take it lightly."},{"games":["SoulSilver","HeartGold"],"text":"You can tell its age by the length of its iron horns. It claims an entire mountain as its territory."},{"games":["LeafGreen","FireRed"],"text":"It claims a large mountain as its sole territory. It mercilessly thrashes those that violate its space."},{"games":["Emerald"],"text":"Its iron horns grow longer a little at a time. They are used to determine the AGGRON’s age. The gouges in its armor are worn with pride as mementos from battles."},{"games":["Sapphire"],"text":"AGGRON is surprisingly protective of its environment. If its mountain is ravaged by a landslide or a fire, this POKéMON will haul topsoil to the area, plant trees, and beautifully restore its own territory."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Sturdy","hidden":false,"description":"The Pokémon cannot be knocked out by a single hit as long as its HP is full. One-hit KO moves wi